WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.163 --> 00:00:17.024
is probably okay, Baloo," Bagheera said.

2
00:00:17.044 --> 00:00:19.745
"He's smart and you've taught him well."

3
00:00:20.666 --> 00:00:22.707
Bagheera licked a paw thoughtfully.

4
00:00:22.727 --> 00:00:27.250
"But we do need a plan to get him back."

5
00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:31.512
"Well, that's a problem," Baloo said.

6
00:00:32.204 --> 00:00:34.926
"Because those monkeys aren't scared of either one of us.

7
00:00:37.248 --> 00:00:39.669
Hey!" He sat up with a jerk.

8
00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:42.871
"The monkeys are afraid of Kaa.

9
00:00:43.592 --> 00:00:44.713
Let's go talk to him!"

10
00:00:44.733 --> 00:00:49.256
"I don't really like talking to the python.

11
00:00:50.136 --> 00:00:51.758
I'm not sure he's our friend.

12
00:00:52.458 --> 00:00:54.860
And Bagheera shuddered.

13
00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:57.842
"He has spooky eyes."

14
00:00:57.862 --> 00:01:00.784
"Come on, Bagheera.

15
00:01:01.056 --> 00:01:02.617
Kaa is very cunning.

16
00:01:03.077 --> 00:01:04.758
Let's go see if he can help us."

17
00:01:05.699 --> 00:01:06.739
Bagheera sighed.

18
00:01:06.759 --> 00:01:15.164
"Fine." Kaa lay on a warm rock in the afternoon sun.

19
00:01:16.144 --> 00:01:19.586
His long body was twisted into coils and curves.

20
00:01:20.527 --> 00:01:23.748
He was admiring his new brown and yellow skin.

21
00:01:23.768 --> 00:01:30.432
"Be careful, Bagheera," Baloo whispered as they approached.

22
00:01:32.628 --> 00:01:36.831
"Kaa is always a little blind after he has changed his skin.

23
00:01:37.591 --> 00:01:39.313
This makes him quick to strike."

24
00:01:40.613 --> 00:01:47.018
Kaa was not a poisonous snake, but he was still very dangerous.

25
00:01:48.038 --> 00:01:52.101
He could coil tightly around someone in a deadly squeeze.

26
00:01:52.121 --> 00:01:54.463
"Good day, Kaa!"

27
00:01:54.803 --> 00:01:55.724
Baloo called.

28
00:01:55.744 --> 00:02:01.728
"Oh, Baloo, what are you doing here?"

29
00:02:07.308 --> 00:02:10.431
"We came to ask for your help," the bear replied.

30
00:02:10.451 --> 00:02:13.073
"We need to find the monkeys.

31
00:02:13.793 --> 00:02:15.335
It's a bit of an emergency."

32
00:02:15.355 --> 00:02:20.178
"Sss." Kaa let out a lazy hiss.

33
00:02:20.198 --> 00:02:23.701
"I'm tired and full.

34
00:02:24.382 --> 00:02:27.925
I'm in no mood to chase monkeys right now."

35
00:02:29.146 --> 00:02:31.307
Baloo flashed a look at Bagheera.

36
00:02:32.088 --> 00:02:33.749
What if Kaa wouldn't help them?

37
00:02:33.769 --> 00:02:38.416
"Um, Kaa Bagheera swallowed.

38
00:02:38.436 --> 00:02:44.579
"Did you know that the monkeys call you a footless yellow earthworm?"

39
00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.641
Kaa's eyes flashed with anger.

40
00:02:48.661 --> 00:02:52.022
"They call me an earthworm?"

41
00:02:52.042 --> 00:02:55.383
"Something like that," Bagheera replied.

42
00:02:55.403 --> 00:03:00.745
"And sometimes they make fun of you," Baloo chimed in.

43
00:03:00.765 --> 00:03:03.687
"They say you have no teeth.

44
00:03:04.387 --> 00:03:06.988
And you're afraid of goats' horns."

45
00:03:08.756 --> 00:03:12.519
"What?" Kaa coiled up tightly.

46
00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:17.944
The big swallowing muscles on his throat rippled and bulged.

47
00:03:18.664 --> 00:03:21.227
"Why are you looking for the monkeys?"

48
00:03:21.247 --> 00:03:27.031
"Well, as you know, I am the man cub's teacher," Baloo began.

49
00:03:27.051 --> 00:03:33.517
"He usually listens to me, but once, he—" Bagheera was getting impatient.

50
00:03:34.077 --> 00:03:36.319
They didn't have time for long stories.

51
00:03:38.964 --> 00:03:41.746
"The trouble is this, Kaa," he said, jumping in.

52
00:03:41.766 --> 00:03:45.868
"Those silly nut-stealers have stolen away the man cub."

53
00:03:46.948 --> 00:03:49.950
"He's a wonderful man cub," Baloo said.

54
00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:55.353
"Mowgli is the smartest and boldest of all the man cubs in the world.

55
00:03:56.353 --> 00:03:59.815
I—we—love him, Kaa."

56
00:03:59.835 --> 00:04:04.878
"Ssss!" Kaa wove his head back and forth.

57
00:04:05.998 --> 00:04:10.345
"The man cub belongs with you—not those monkeys.

58
00:04:10.866 --> 00:04:12.527
You are his family."

59
00:04:13.488 --> 00:04:15.450
"That's why we're here," Bagheera said.

60
00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:20.394
"The monkeys are afraid of only one animal in the jungle—you."

61
00:04:20.414 --> 00:04:25.598
"So we're hoping you'll help us find them," Baloo added.

62
00:04:26.459 --> 00:04:33.765
"Please." "Those horrible monkeys chatter constantly," Kaa muttered.

63
00:04:33.785 --> 00:04:37.108
"And they are foolish and lazy."

64
00:04:38.508 --> 00:04:40.028
He swung toward Bagheera.

65
00:04:40.048 --> 00:04:44.390
"What do the monkeys call me—a yellow fish?"

66
00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:46.850
Bagheera lowered his head.

67
00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:48.951
"A yellow earthworm.

68
00:04:49.591 --> 00:04:51.012
And other terrible names."

69
00:04:51.032 --> 00:04:57.273
"I'm going to remind them to speak well of me!"

70
00:04:57.753 --> 00:04:58.654
Kaa snapped.

71
00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:00.874
"Where did they go?"

72
00:05:00.894 --> 00:05:05.676
"We thought you might know, Kaa," Baloo said.

73
00:05:06.988 --> 00:05:10.691
"I do know they moved to a different part of the jungle today."

74
00:05:10.711 --> 00:05:12.393
Kaa hissed.

75
00:05:13.353 --> 00:05:17.016
"I heard them laughing among the treetops earlier.

76
00:05:17.657 --> 00:05:19.318
But I—" "Up!

77
00:05:19.939 --> 00:05:22.841
Up!" A sharp cry came from above.

78
00:05:23.742 --> 00:05:24.703
Baloo looked up.

79
00:05:26.184 --> 00:05:28.426
Rann was flying across the sky.

80
00:05:28.446 --> 00:05:31.108
"I have a message from Mowgli!"

81
00:05:31.388 --> 00:05:32.309
the hawk cried.

82
00:05:32.329 --> 00:05:35.732
"The monkeys have carried him deep into the jungle.

83
00:05:36.576 --> 00:05:39.460
He is now beyond the river—in Monkey City!"
